==English==
{{was wotd|2016|July|30}}

===Alternative forms===
{{wp}}
[[File:Path leading to the John F. Kennedy Memorial, Runnymede, UK - 20150708-08.JPG|thumb|Setts ''(sense 5)'' in the path leading to the [[w:Runnymede#John F. Kennedy Memorial|John F. Kennedy Memorial]] at [[Runnymede]] in [[Surrey]], [[England]], United Kingdom]]
* {{alt|en|set}}

===Etymology===
A variant of {{m|en|set}} to distinguish various technical senses.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sĕt}}, {{IPA|en|/sɛt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-set.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|set}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|badger tunnel}} The system of [[tunnel]]s that is the home of a [[badger]].
#: {{hyper|en|burrow|earth|warren}}
#: {{near-syn|en|cete}}
# The pattern of distinctive [[thread]]s and [[yarn]]s that make up the [[plaid]] of a [[Scottish]] [[tartan]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=J. Charles Thompson|mainauthor=James Grant|title=Scottish Tartans in Full Color|chapter=Introduction|text=The ''Vestiarium'' gave '''setts''' for Lowland houses as well as Highland clans{{...}}and many families within the clans have their own '''setts''' to add to the clan tartans.{{...}}The clans and families are branching out with Dress and Hunting tartans, and the same '''sett'''—any '''sett'''—may be produced in dark "modern," lighter "ancient" or "muted" color schemes.}}
# {{lb|en|weaving}} The number of [[warp]] [[end]]s per [[inch]] in the [[cloth]].
#: {{syn|en|sley}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Handwoven|year=2026|volume=XLVII|number=1|page=45|title=Flights of Fancy|author=Malynda Allen
|text=To achieve a balanced weave, the '''sett''' must be a little tighter than it would be for a twill.}}
# {{lb|en|weaving|England}} The number of [[reed]]s or [[split]]s per [[inch]] – one half the number of [[end]]s per [[inch]].
# {{senseid|en|stone}} A small, square-cut piece of [[quarry#Verb|quarried]] stone used for [[pave|paving]] and [[edge#Verb|edging]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Belgian block}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Joseph Conrad|chapter=7|chapterurl=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/A_Personal_Record/Chapter_VII|title=w:A Personal Record|location=New York, N.Y.; London|publisher=[[w:Harper (publisher)|Harper & Bros. Publishers]]|year=1912|oclc=18964862|passage=Three horses trotted abreast, with the clatter of hoofs on the granite '''setts''', and the yellow, uproarious machine jolted violently behind them, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=[[w:Tim Richardson (writer)|Tim Richardson]]|title=The JFK memorial at Runnymede is fit to stand forever: Sir {{w|Geoffrey Jellicoe}}'s wonderful tribute to [[w:John F. Kennedy|JFK]] at Runnymede hinges on the power of landscape [print edition: A memorial to JFK fit to stand forever]|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/gardening/gardenstovisit/10451578/The-JFK-memorial-at-Runnymede-is-fit-to-stand-forever.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150703034638/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/gardening/gardenstovisit/10451578/The-JFK-memorial-at-Runnymede-is-fit-to-stand-forever.html|archivedate=3 July 2015|newspaper={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Gardening)|date=16 November 2013|page=G8|passage=This path, which consists of some 60,000 '''setts''' laid directly into the earth, is perhaps the single most noteworthy 'feature' of the design, lending the whole conception a feeling of unity and coherence, enhancing the sense that one has been absorbed into both the place and the journey through it.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A mine or set of mines on [[lease]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1857|journal=The Mining Magazine|page=128
|passage={{...}} let the dialler, with the same instrument he uses underground, run a north and south line on the surface, in any convenient part of the '''sett''', marking the extremities by well-fixed points, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A collection of pumps in a mine.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1898|publisher=Institution of Mining Engineers|location=Great Britain|journal=The Mining Engineer|page=196
|passage=After a delay of about three months, the 24 inches '''sett''' of pumps was ready for work, and sinking was resumed with one sett of pumps 18 inches in diameter in No. 1 pit, and one sett 24 inches in diameter in No. 2 pit; {{...}}}}
# {{obs form|en|set||group}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Education|page=260|text=The Father cannot stay any longer for the Portion, nor the Mother for a new '''Sett''' of Babies to play with {{...}}}}

